MPM Multi-Omics Biomarker Knowledge Graph System Project Specification


Malignant pleural mesothelioma (MPM) is a highly aggressive pleural tumor, and research on MPM involves extensive gene, protein, signaling pathway, drug, and disease information scattered 
across various databases and scientific literature. Due to inconsistencies in data formats, discrepancies in entity naming, and fragmented relationship information among different data sources, 
researchers face significant challenges in rapidly integrating and querying molecular mechanisms related to MPM.


This project aims to develop a multi-omics biomarker knowledge graph system dedicated to MPM research. By integrating diverse biomedical data types—including genes, proteins, pathways, drugs, 
diseases, and publications—the system establishes a unified data model and an interconnected network of biological entities. Leveraging standardized database information and evidence from scientific 
literature, the system builds a reliable data foundation and utilizes Neo4j, a graph database, to store, query, and visualize complex biomedical relationships.


The final system offers functionalities such as entity search, relationship exploration, multi-hop path queries, literature evidence retrieval, and closed-loop analysis of drug-target-disease 
associations. It provides robust data support for MPM-related biomarker research, discovery of potential therapeutic targets, and subsequent AI-enhanced analytical applications.
